<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Upper Hungary</h1><p class="st-meta">1682 CE – 1685 CE · capital Kassa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ottoman-backed realm of the Kuruc rebel Imre Thököly in what is now eastern Slovakia, which collapsed with the Ottoman defeat at Vienna.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imre-thokoly">Imre Thököly</a>, a Lutheran noble, led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a> rebels of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> persecution of Protestants from 1678. After a string of victories he captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice">Kassa</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-hungary">Upper Hungary</a>, and in 1682 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehmed-iv">Mehmed IV</a> recognised him as king of Upper Hungary in return for tribute; Thököly himself used the title of prince.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imre-thokoly">Thököly</a> governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice">Kassa</a> through diets of the northern counties, protecting Lutheran and Calvinist worship and paying the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> an annual tribute. His power rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a> troops of minor nobles, peasants and haiduks. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilona-zrinyi">Ilona Zrínyi</a>, widow of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> Rákóczi, brought him the great Rákóczi estates and the castle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukachevo">Munkács</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imre-thokoly">Thököly</a> supported the Ottoman siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1683, and after its failure <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> armies retook his towns. In 1685 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> arrested him and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosice">Kassa</a> fell. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilona-zrinyi">Ilona Zrínyi</a> held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukachevo">Munkács</a> until 1688. Thököly died in exile in Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izmit">Izmit</a> in 1705.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-upper-hungary.jpg" alt="Principality of Upper Hungary" width="320" height="207"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thokoly_imre_zaszlaja.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1682 CE – 1685 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kassa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Imre Thököly</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestant and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hungarian, Slovak</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Thököly's Upper Hungary, Kingdom of Upper Hungary</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1684&amp;focus=principality-of-upper-hungary" aria-label="Principality of Upper Hungary on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5172 476 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Upper Hungary lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5492 732L5398 749M5492 732L5709 970M5492 732L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5398 749h0M5709 970h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5492 732h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5492 732h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1684&amp;focus=principality-of-upper-hungary">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
